---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
---

<BaseLayout
  title="About"
  description="What Komadrona Review is, why it exists, how it works, who maintains it, and how contributors and sources are credited."
>
  <header class="page-header">
    <div class="container">
      <span class="eyebrow">About the project</span>
      <h1>A clearer way to review, without pretending to be official.</h1>
      <p>
        Komadrona Review is an independent, source-based study and practice project for aspiring Philippine midwives.
        It is being built to make reviewer material easier to navigate, verify, revisit, and correct.
      </p>
    </div>
  </header>

  <section class="section" style="padding-top: 1rem;">
    <div class="container hero-grid">
      <article class="prose" style="padding-bottom: 0;">
        <span class="eyebrow">What it is</span>
        <h2>A structured study companion</h2>
        <p>
          The project organizes review material around the principal subjects identified in the current referenced
          PRC Midwives Licensure Examination program. Topics will use traceable laws, official Philippine health and
          education publications, current guidance, and documented corrections.
        </p>
        <p>
          Review articles, practice questions, bookmarks, and locally recorded progress are intended to work together
          as one simple study environment. Version 1 remains static and does not require an account.
        </p>
      </article>

      <aside class="panel legal-gate" aria-labelledby="project-status">
        <span class="badge">Foundation release</span>
        <h2 id="project-status" style="margin-top: 1rem;">Current status</h2>
        <ul>
          <li>Legal, privacy, source, and licensing foundation implemented</li>
          <li>Five review-domain structure prepared</li>
          <li>Reference registry established</li>
          <li>Reviewer articles and practice forms still in development</li>
        </ul>
        <a class="button button-secondary" href="/sources">View the source register</a>
      </aside>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section section-muted" aria-labelledby="why-komadrona">
    <div class="container">
      <div class="section-heading">
        <span class="eyebrow">Why it exists</span>
        <h2 id="why-komadrona">Review material should be traceable.</h2>
        <p>
          Many study resources circulate as screenshots, copied answer sets, anonymous notes, or claims without a
          visible source. Komadrona Review takes a slower approach: identify the source, explain the concept originally,
          record when it was checked, and correct it when necessary.
        </p>
      </div>

      <div class="card-grid">
        <article class="card">
          <h3>Source-based</h3>
          <p>
            Articles and questions must point to an official law, issuance, guideline, or other accepted reference.
            AI-generated text and social-media claims are not treated as final authorities.
          </p>
        </article>

        <article class="card">
          <h3>Independent</h3>
          <p>
            The project is not affiliated with or endorsed by PRC, the Board of Midwifery, DOH, CHED, any school, or
            any review center. Institutional names appear only for accurate attribution.
          </p>
        </article>

        <article class="card">
          <h3>Correctable</h3>
          <p>
            Content carries a review status and source-check date. Outdated or disputed material can be marked for
            re-verification instead of silently remaining in circulation.
          </p>
        </article>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section" aria-labelledby="personal-origin">
    <div class="container hero-grid">
      <div class="section-heading">
        <span class="eyebrow">Personal origin</span>
        <h2 id="personal-origin">It started with Kathy.</h2>
        <p>
          A major personal motivation behind Komadrona Review is Kathy, who is currently in her fourth year of
          midwifery studies. Her journey gave the project a real person and purpose to build around: not simply another
          collection of notes, but a reviewer careful enough to be genuinely useful to someone carrying the pressure,
          detail, and responsibility of the program.
        </p>
      </div>

      <article class="card">
        <span class="badge">Learning while building</span>
        <h3 style="margin-top: 1rem;">Built as a developer and a student</h3>
        <p>
          I am also studying midwifery while developing this site. That means the project is being shaped from both
          sides: as a developer designing the system and as a learner working through the same subjects, sources,
          questions, and uncertainties that the site is meant to organize.
        </p>
        <p>
          What began as something I wanted to make for Kathy is being developed openly so it can become useful to other
          aspiring midwives as well.
        </p>
        <p class="small-print">
          Kathy is acknowledged as the project's major personal inspiration, not as a technical contributor or
          clinical reviewer.
        </p>
      </article>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section section-muted" aria-labelledby="for-whom">
    <div class="container">
      <div class="section-heading">
        <span class="eyebrow">Who it is for</span>
        <h2 id="for-whom">Built for independent learners.</h2>
        <p>
          Komadrona Review is designed primarily for students and graduates reviewing Philippine midwifery concepts,
          especially learners who need a mobile-friendly resource that remains usable without creating an account.
        </p>
      </div>

      <div class="card-grid">
        <article class="card">
          <h3>Study by subject</h3>
          <p>Move through structured domains and topic pages rather than an unorganized collection of answer sheets.</p>
        </article>

        <article class="card">
          <h3>Practice repeatedly</h3>
          <p>Use original practice quizzes with explanations and unlimited retries after the forms are reviewed.</p>
        </article>

        <article class="card">
          <h3>Track privately</h3>
          <p>Keep completion, bookmarks, and self-recorded scores in the browser without a central learner database.</p>
        </article>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section" aria-labelledby="boundaries">
    <div class="container hero-grid">
      <div class="section-heading">
        <span class="eyebrow">Project boundaries</span>
        <h2 id="boundaries">What it is not</h2>
        <p>
          Clear limits are part of the project design. Komadrona Review should never look more authoritative than the
          evidence and review work behind it.
        </p>
      </div>

      <ul class="status-list">
        <li>Not an official PRC reviewer</li>
        <li>Not medical or patient-specific advice</li>
        <li>Not a replacement for clinical supervision</li>
        <li>Not a passing-score guarantee</li>
        <li>Not a repository of recalled board questions</li>
        <li>Not an official educational record</li>
      </ul>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section section-muted" aria-labelledby="credits">
    <div class="container">
      <div class="section-heading">
        <span class="eyebrow">Credits and attribution</span>
        <h2 id="credits">People behind the project</h2>
        <p>Credits are based on actual work performed and consent to be named.</p>
      </div>

      <div class="card-grid two-column">
        <article class="card">
          <span class="badge">Creator</span>
          <h3 style="margin-top: 1rem;">Kirch Ivan A. Balite</h3>
          <p><strong>Creator, developer, researcher, student, and maintainer</strong></p>
          <p>
            Responsible for project direction, architecture, interface design, source governance, implementation, and
            release maintenance while undertaking his own midwifery studies.
          </p>
          <p class="small-print">Independent educational project based in Bohol, Philippines.</p>
        </article>

        <article class="card">
          <span class="badge">Clinical review</span>
          <h3 style="margin-top: 1rem;">No public reviewer credited yet</h3>
          <p>
            Qualified reviewers will be listed only after completing a documented review of identified material and
            consenting to public attribution.
          </p>
          <p>
            Informal advice, friendship, employment, school affiliation, or being asked a question does not make a
            person responsible for the project or qualify them for a reviewer credit.
          </p>
        </article>
      </div>

      <div class="card-grid" style="margin-top: 1rem;">
        <article class="card">
          <h3>Code and accessibility contributors</h3>
          <p>
            Accepted contributors may be credited for code, testing, accessibility, research, editing, documentation,
            or corrections. Their contribution does not imply responsibility for the complete website.
          </p>
        </article>

        <article class="card">
          <h3>Source institutions</h3>
          <p>
            PRC, the Professional Regulatory Board of Midwifery, DOH, CHED, WHO, Congress, and other publishers are
            credited through citations. Citation does not imply endorsement or approval.
          </p>
        </article>

        <article class="card">
          <h3>Brand and publication ownership</h3>
          <p>
            Agency names, institutional names, trademarks, seals, and third-party publications remain the property of
            their respective owners. Komadrona Review does not claim ownership over them.
          </p>
        </article>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section" aria-labelledby="licensing">
    <div class="container hero-grid">
      <div class="section-heading">
        <span class="eyebrow">Open project</span>
        <h2 id="licensing">Licensing and contributions</h2>
        <p>
          The website source code is published under the MIT License. Original educational articles, original practice
          questions, and original illustrations use the project content license unless a page states otherwise.
        </p>
      </div>

      <div class="card">
        <h3>Contribute carefully</h3>
        <p>
          Contributions must be original, source-backed, privacy-safe, and free of confidential or proprietary
          examination content. Medical material is not considered clinically reviewed merely because it was submitted.
        </p>
        <div class="action-row">
          <a class="button button-secondary" href="/credits">Detailed credits policy</a>
          <a class="button button-secondary" href="/disclaimer">Read project limitations</a>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>
</BaseLayout>
